  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Central Pacific Submarine Fiber Optic Cable System Feasibility Study, through APTelecom</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A USTDA grant funds a feasibility study (Study) for Tuvalu Telecom Corporation to assess the technical and commercial viability of a 15,900-kilometer Central Pacific submarine fiberoptic cable system with trunk lines between Guam and American Samoa that would provide new or expanded connectivity to 14 Pacific Island countries and overseas territories. U.S. advisory firm, APTelecom LLC will carry out the Study on a sole-source basis.</narrative>
  </description>
